 "question": "What does the build cylinder fit into?",
 "before": {
  "answer": "The build base fits inside the build cylinder: the BOM says the base should be about 1 mm smaller in radius, and gives the cylinder ID as 252 and the base as Ø250; the drawings show Ø252 and Ø250 respectively [BOM.47.design_intent] [BOM.46.design_intent] [D-023.p1.vision.c10] [D-024.p1.a08]. A ceramic seal sits in the base’s groove against the cylinder wall [Zaxis_legend.l07] [Zaxis_legend.l06].\n\nCaution: the cylinder drawing’s Ø262,0 H7 and Ø264,0 H7 callouts fail the ISO 286 check, so those readings are probably wrong and don’t establish the fit [D-023.p1.vision.c06] [D-023.p1.vision.c07].",
